# Which files are sensitive enough to want a second pair of eyes, and which are
# not. Content is not listed here: an announcement, a set of minutes or a roster
# change publishes without review, which is the whole point of the editor.
#
# What is listed is the machinery — how the site is built, deployed, and
# presented to the person editing it. A change here can stop the site
# publishing, or publish something nobody meant to.
#
# ⚠ NOTHING ENFORCES THIS YET, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.
#
# The branch protection rule that would enforce it requires a review from a code
# owner, and GitHub does not accept a code owner's approval of their own pull
# request. On a repository with one maintainer that rule blocks every change,
# including the maintainer's own — the same trap as a review queue on ordinary
# content, arriving by a different door.
#
# So this file records the intent and waits. Enable "Require review from Code
# Owners" on the default branch at the point a second person holds write access,
# which is execution plan task 6.2.

/.github/                 @shelbybaird
/static/admin/config.yml  @shelbybaird
/hugo.toml                @shelbybaird
